{
  "evidenceId": "ev-20261011-pen-speed-ema",
  "date": "2026-10-11",
  "claim": "RawAccel's input-speed EMA does not fix the RawAccel engine's report-timing gain noise on the pen: across 0.5-5 ms half-lives it lowers the aim-band noise std by at most ~30% (Psylocke 17.1% -> 11.9% at 5 ms) while the worst single-report gain error - the spike a player feels - does not improve (Psylocke 69.7% raw, 63-71% smoothed), and it delays the gain on a flick from rest (up to 0.8 mm of the first 30 ms delivered at the wrong gain at 5 ms). Cadence Lock removes the same noise to 0.000% with no lag. The 2026-09-16 decision to keep the pen's speed EMAs at 0 stands; Cadence Lock remains the answer for steep-ramp cards.",
  "method": "SpeedEmaLab (AimForge --ema-lab): RawAccel's linear_ema_smoother ported line for line from RawAccelOfficial/rawaccel common/rawaccel.hpp (master 53a7213, 2025-07-27; input trend half-life 1.25 ms, dampening 0.75), fed the per-report speed from arrival-time dt. Aim band: CadenceLab's stream (25 mm amplitude, 1.5 Hz, 6 s, 360 Hz, 0.01 mm lattice, +/-10% arrival jitter), scored 55-220 mm/s. Flick: 200 ms rest then 300 mm/s. Tap: 40 mm/s for 60 ms. The user's RawAccel is 1.7.0; the port is from master - the smoother is assumed unchanged since 1.7 (UNVERIFIED against the 1.7.0 tag).",
